WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:04.460
Horror movies might be filled with frights,
but they're usually pretty fun to watch, too.

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:08.170
Every now and again, however, there comes
along a scary movie that's so disturbing it's

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:10.960
hard to justify ever sitting through it again.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:15.280
From extreme brutality to the true emotional torment
of audiences, these are the movies you'll

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:18.040
want to opt out of re-visiting after the first
run.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.960
As always, beware the spoilers.

00:00:19.960 --> 00:00:21.720
The Sacrament

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:26.800
Loosely based on true events, The Sacrament
is excruciatingly tense and takes the story

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.710
and its characters to some incredibly dark
places.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:33.899
The faux-documentary features three reporters
investigating a new religious movement in

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:34.899
Africa.

00:00:34.899 --> 00:00:39.289
And the climax depicts the ritual self-sacrifice
of the cult members, which does not flinch

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:43.469
from a single moment of the pain, confusion,
and fear they experience.

00:00:43.469 --> 00:00:48.109
It gets particularly difficult to watch when
one of the reporters is tied down by his sister

00:00:48.109 --> 00:00:50.640
and forced to participate in the ritual with
her.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:55.050
In terms of craft, The Sacrament probably
is an incredibly well done movie.

00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:56.120
"I tried.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.260
God knows I tried."

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:01.949
But once you've watched the film and know
the places it will take you to, it's almost

00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:04.760
impossible to watch again.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:05.760
Martyrs

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:08.840
The "torture-horror" subgenre hit a new benchmark
with Martyrs.

00:01:08.840 --> 00:01:13.729
The French film features characters experiencing
every kind of agony imaginable, from suffering

00:01:13.729 --> 00:01:15.990
intense beatings to being flayed alive.

00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:20.299
And it's the existential justification for
this cycle of sinister acts that's really

00:01:20.299 --> 00:01:21.320
hard to bear.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:25.369
The tormentors are attempting to gain knowledge
of the afterlife by turning their subjects

00:01:25.369 --> 00:01:28.210
into martyrs who are abused into transcendance.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:32.310
And after so much anguish and gruesome violence,
audiences are ultimately left to wonder what

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:34.719
the experience revealed, if anything.

00:01:34.719 --> 00:01:39.500
It's an experience to watch this movie unfold,
but it is also an exhausting one for sure.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:40.909
Funny Games

00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:44.970
Sometimes bad things happen to good people
and there's no rhyme or reason to it.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:47.500
Funny Games is a story about this very idea.

00:01:47.500 --> 00:01:52.220
Two sociopathic youths, Peter and Paul, stage
a physical and emotional assault on a family

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:53.299
in their own home.

00:01:53.299 --> 00:01:54.340
Bones are broken.

00:01:54.340 --> 00:01:55.350
Lives are ended.

00:01:55.350 --> 00:01:57.399
A dog goes to doggy heaven.

00:01:57.399 --> 00:02:01.049
And all of this is done in service of a sick
game being played by the boys.

00:02:01.049 --> 00:02:04.090
There is no backstory between the family and
the men torturing them.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:07.859
It's not a revenge scheme, and there is no
plot twist revealing the boys to be the abandoned

00:02:07.859 --> 00:02:09.729
children of the mother or the father.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:14.569
Peter and Paul simply show up, commit countless
atrocities, and then move on to the next family.

00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:18.840
Funny Games might be tremendously made, but
it is a horrifying film that presents sick

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:23.500
joy in senseless violence and probably won't
leave you reaching for the DVD again any time

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.560
soon.

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:25.959
The Invitation

00:02:25.959 --> 00:02:29.940
Even without its twist ending, The Invitation
would be uncomfortable to sit through a second

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:30.940
time.

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:35.200
The film sets out to put the nuance of interactions
between lapsed friends under a microscope.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:39.060
Through a few hours spent at a tense dinner
party, it analyzes the minute intricacies

00:02:39.060 --> 00:02:41.690
of every awkward exchange between characters.

00:02:41.690 --> 00:02:45.840
And it explores the efforts people will go
through to save face and stifle survival instincts

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:48.200
when cordial social interactions go to places
they shouldn't.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:51.599
"Don't you guys think this is a little bit
weird?"

00:02:51.599 --> 00:02:55.080
Furthermore, it's a stunning meditation on
grief and what people will do to cope with

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:56.080
loss.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.400
These themes are explored very nicely, but
they're so heavy that a second viewing is

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.490
likely out of the question for most moviegoers.

00:03:01.490 --> 00:03:05.799
And this is all before the film's third act,
which features the host couple trying to snuff

00:03:05.799 --> 00:03:09.610
out all their friends and then off themselves
in the name of a mysterious spiritual group

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:10.610
they've joined.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:15.810
All in all, it's an immaculate film that is
probably best left alone after a single viewing.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:16.810
Lake Mungo

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:20.739
There are points at which Lake Mungo hardly
feels like a horror film.

00:03:20.739 --> 00:03:25.049
The imitation-documentary plays out as a look
into how the loss of a loved one can devastate

00:03:25.049 --> 00:03:26.910
the people around them over time.

00:03:26.910 --> 00:03:30.390
There are supernatural elements to the film
and some great frights to be had, but they're

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:33.790
comparatively sparse across the movie's hour
and a half running time.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:37.840
Those scares aren't what will keep viewers
from coming back for a second viewing, though.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.069
That falls entirely on the subject matter.

00:03:40.069 --> 00:03:44.099
By staging the film as a documentary with
no well-known actors to lower the audience's

00:03:44.099 --> 00:03:48.760
suspension of disbelief, director Joel Anderson
amplifies the emotional devastation the Palmer

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:52.030
family experiences after the loss of their
daughter Alice.

00:03:52.030 --> 00:03:55.489
And that plays directly into the supernatural
aspects of the plot, too.

00:03:55.489 --> 00:03:59.799
Lake Mungo is a superb film, but one that
deals with some very heavy subject matter

00:03:59.799 --> 00:04:03.140
and would be very hard to sit through a second
time.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:04.140
Audition

00:04:04.140 --> 00:04:09.140
Takashi Miike has released over 100 films,
and he could probably go on to direct 100

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:12.510
more with not one of them earning the reputation
that Audition has.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:16.609
It's the story of a widower who, at the urging
of his son, connects with a young woman named

00:04:16.609 --> 00:04:17.609
Asami.

00:04:17.609 --> 00:04:21.310
As their romance develops, it becomes clear
that there is more to her than she lets on.

00:04:21.310 --> 00:04:25.570
Suspicions build slowly towards the film's
serious climax, which features a horrific scene

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:30.550
of torture and a mutilated man Asami sadistically
keeps alive in a bag.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:34.470
Other films featuring torture might try to
shock the audience with a wide array of methods,

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:39.280
but Miike instead pares it down to one excruciatingly
simple, prolonged moment of pain.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:43.180
Audition is a masterpiece, no doubt about
it, and it's absolutely worth seeing.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:46.420
But it's still a hard movie to get through
the first time around, and knowing what the

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:50.000
end holds will not make rewatching it any
easier.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:51.000
Thanks for watching!

